\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Plaquette order for affine links}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{The [plaquette holonomy](fdip-006N) multiplies edge transports with
the first factor on the right, and a reversed edge contributes the
inverse. \ref{fdip-006F} uses the same order for the holonomy of a
path. The notes that follow keep that order. The structure group is
the group of affine links in \ref{fdip-00OB}, built from the Clifford
group of a quadratic module of any rank. The cells are those of a
[finite cubical 2-complex](fdip-006M). The Wilson trace is outside
this construction.}
